@startuml fmm-maturity-ladder
!theme plain
title FHIR Maturity Model — Progression for a FHIR IG

state "FMM 0" as s0 #FFECB3 : CI build only.\nArtifact exists and builds cleanly.

state "FMM 1" as s1 #FFF9C4 : CI build / draft ballot eligible.\nWork Group considers substantially complete.\nNo unresolved blocking issues.

state "FMM 2" as s2 #E8F5E9 : STU ballot eligible.\nInteroperability demonstrated in ≥ 3 independent systems.\nConnectathon results accepted by FMG.

state "FMM 3" as s3 #DCEDC8 : STU Release 1.\nPassed STU ballot.\nBroad review with non-trivial changes from external feedback.

state "FMM 4" as s4 #C8E6C9 : STU Release 2+.\nEvidence of broad review.\nMultiple independent implementations.\nBreaking changes slowing significantly.

state "FMM 5" as s5 #B2EBF2 : Normative ballot eligible.\n≥ 2 formal release cycles at FMM 1+.\n≥ 5 independent production systems.\nFor international IGs: implementations in > 1 country.

[*] --> s0
s0 --> s1 : artifact matures
s1 --> s2 : Connectathon\nevidence accepted
s2 --> s3 : STU ballot passed
s3 --> s4 : subsequent STU cycles
s4 --> s5 : production evidence\n+ semantic stability
s5 --> [*] : Normative ballot\n+ publication

@enduml
